invariant: INV-26
file: gcm.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: an AES=runtime QUIC object hands the whole passes of a seal or
  an open under a schedule the table runs to gcm_hw.c's one-pass loops,
  so a session whose caller's probe found no AES instructions executes
  them and the carry-less multiply on every Initial packet it seals or
  opens past 128 bytes, and dies of SIGILL on the CPU that probe
  described. Both paths compute
  the same bytes, so no vector notices. gcm.c's instruction_rounds asserts
  that its schedule runs on the instructions, and bin/aes_runtime_test
  seals RFC 9001's Initial packets under the absent answer, so the
  assertion stops that binary.

--- old
    if (!on_instructions(k)) {
        return 0;
    }
#endif
    size_t pass_bytes = (size_t)GCM_HW_PASS_BLOCKS * AES_BLOCK;
--- new
    if (k == NULL) {
        return 0;
    }
#endif
    size_t pass_bytes = (size_t)GCM_HW_PASS_BLOCKS * AES_BLOCK;
